# Example fixture: Si(111) slab, same generation as si111_slab.fdf but
# termination index 1 -- the other symmetric option pymatgen's
# SlabGenerator finds, which splits through a strongly-bonded bilayer
# instead of the weakly-bonded gap between bilayers. Each of the 8 surface
# atoms is missing 3 bonds (coordination 1 instead of the bulk value 4),
# not 1 -- geometrically underdetermined from local coordination alone (with
# only 1 existing bond vector, there are infinitely many ways to place 3
# more without extra symmetry assumptions). Used to exercise
# stb-passivate's "needs manual attention" warning path: expect 0 atoms
# auto-passivated and 8 reported as unresolved, atom count unchanged (32).

NumberOfSpecies    1
NumberofAtoms      32

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   14   Si
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 5.43000000   0.00000000   -5.43000000
 -0.00000000   5.43000000   -5.43000000
 0.00000000   0.00000000   43.44000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
